CORE-PARITY-AUDIT/

# Build artifacts must not be tracked. Five stale copies of the node binary
# (blockbrew.w13, .w13b, .pre-w13, .pre-w13-recovery, .462c233-deployed) plus
# two shim binaries were committed here — 156 MB that every clone pays for,
# and an incidental `go build` rewriting a tracked binary trips
# promote_mainnet.sh's dirty-tree refusal at deploy time. Pinned deploy
# binaries belong in deploy/ via tools/promote_mainnet.sh, not in the source
# tree. (Untracking does not shrink an existing clone — the blobs are still in
# history — but it stops the growth and unblocks the deploy gate.)
blockbrew.w13
blockbrew.w13b
blockbrew.pre-w13
blockbrew.pre-w13-recovery
blockbrew.462c233-deployed
